 in the three months before the base. It then formed a base for about 5 weeks, peaking at $27.28 and pulling back 32% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On Apr 12, 2022 it closed at $29.15, its first close above the base high of $27.28. Volume that day was 12.1M shares, 1.49x the prior 10-day average of 8.2M. It didn't hold. By Apr 25, 2022 it had closed below the breakout level three days running, and the chart ends at $25.20.","lesson":"This is an example of a failed breakout where everything looked right, volume included, and the stock fell back anyway. It happens. This is why traders cut losses fast instead of hoping."}}